Section 3 - Policy Statement
(4)
The University seeks to:
reinforce University’s
Code of Conduct
and our values;
use workforce information in order to effectively and efficiently manage its workforce;
apply the terms and conditions of the
La Trobe University Enterprise Agreement 2023
approved by the Fair Work Commission (‘the Collective Agreement’);
ensure workforce management practices are informed by the strategic and operational requirements of the workplace;
ensure that decisions on workplace relations issues are objective and in accordance with relevant legislation and the
Enterprise Agreement
;
ensure that behaviour demonstrated in the workplace is compliant with legislation, our
Code of Conduct
and other policies/procedures;
ensure working conditions consider staff health and safety and are managed in a strategic manner, complying with legislation, our
Code of Conduct
and other policies/procedures.
